WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.701
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.901
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:05.767
You're here.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.133
Thank you.
-Come on!

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.467
-Let's get to some news, here.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:11.534
Guys, today Elon Musk said
he needs more details

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:14.267
about how many spam accounts are
on Twitter

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:17.434
and, until then,
his $44 billion deal to buy

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.734
is temporarily on hold.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:20.834
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.334
Yep.
Temporarily on hold.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:25.701
When they heard, even Verizon
customer service reps were like,

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:26.934
"Oh, he's not coming back.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.300
[ Laughter ]
Oh, no."

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.567
Elon might be on to something
with the spam accounts.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.067
It's a little odd
that Chef Boyardee

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:34.868
has 800 million
followers, you know.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.567
That's right, Elon Musk's
purchase of Twitter is on hold.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:38.601
In a statement, he said...

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.067
Then Twitter CEO
Jack Dorsey said...

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:48.467
Then Elon said...

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:51.901
And Dorsey said...

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.334
[ Laughter ]
And Elon said...

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:58.133
And Dorsey said...

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.267
[ Muffled ]

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:01.934
Well, we'll see what happens.
-Wow.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:05.334
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:06.968
Hey, this is cool --

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:10.567
On Sunday night,
a total blood moon eclipse

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:12.100
is going to rise over the U.S.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.067
[ Oohs ]

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.934
Yep, a total blood moon eclipse.

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:17.167
It's like every "Twilight" movie
title rolled into one.

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:18.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.567
Very exciting, a red moon.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.100
Or, as Mars put it...

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.367
[ Slow clap ]

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:24.133
"How original."

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:26.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.501
Guys, get this --
apparently, inflation has caused

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.501
a lot of consumers,
including young people,

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.667
to do less online shopping

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:34.367
and now malls are attempting
to get young people

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.767
to go shopping again,

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.167
but I think they're trying
a little too hard.

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.234
Look at this commercial
I saw today.

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:42.300
[ Vuvuzela blasts ]
Online shopping is dank.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.100
But you know what's always
savage? Malls.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.367
-[Electronic voice reverberates]
-That's right.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.434
Forget Prime.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:49.033
We got a fountain full of dimes.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.400
-And pennies.
-So, yassify your drip

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.968
at all the tope stores, like...

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:56.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.267
Spencer Gifts.

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:00.334
-No parents allowed.

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.267
-Plus...

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.367
[ Laughter ]
Oh, and if you're actually...

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:07.601
hit up that Jamba.

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:11.000
[ Laughter ]
And did I mention
the escalators?

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.033
[ Ethereal tune plays ]

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.834
So don't be a simp.

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:16.934
Get some free samps

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:18.200
-[ Screech ]
-at Panda Express,

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.067
make Sbarro your sbae,

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:20.968
and go straight-up...

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.100
-[ Screeching ]

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.267
Yeah.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:30.067
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:36.000
Hey, listen to this -- the USDA
has issued a public health alert

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.968
over ground beef
from Whole Foods

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:41.067
that could contain
plastic fragments.

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.667
[ Oohs ]
On the bright side,
since it's Whole Foods,

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.667
is at least organic,
grass-fed plastic.

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.901
Yep, customers knew there was
plastic when it felt like

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.801
the roof of their mouth
had stepped on a LEGO.

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:52.167
[ Laughter ]
But Whole Foods
isn't worried now.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:55.000
They're selling it as a Real
Impossible Burger, yeah.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:58.567
Hey, this is cool --
I saw that Google just unveiled

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.400
prototype glasses
that can actually

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.133
translate languages for you
in real time.

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:04.801
[ Murmuring ]
Basically, someone could speak
a different language

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.934
and the translation
will appear on your lens.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.033
Take a look at this.
It's real.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:12.133
♪♪

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:14.234
-You should be seeing
what I'm saying,

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:17.000
just transcribed for you
in real time,

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.767
kind of like subtitles
for the world.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:20.801
-Isn't that cool?

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.501
[ Murmuring ]
Yeah.
-Wow.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.734
Not only that, apparently,
the glasses can also translate

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:26.000
what people actually mean

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.267
when they say certain phrases
to you in English.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:29.434
[ Laughter ]
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:30.734
For instance, if someone says...

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:33.000
It translates to...

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:38.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:40.067
Next up, if someone asks...

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:42.667
It translates to...

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:48.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.234
And, finally, if someone says...

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.033
It translates to...

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.701
[ Laughter and applause ]
It's pretty spot-on.
It's good.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.801
[ Cheering ]

00:03:57.801 --> 00:03:59.501
Hey, I read
that Southwest Airlines

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.100
is spending $2 billion

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.734
to upgrade their planes
with faster Wi-Fi,

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:07.367
charging ports, and larger
overhead bins, yeah.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:08.400
Meanwhile, not to be outdone,

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.234
Spirit Airlines
is adding windows.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:14.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.567
Some entertainment news --
I saw that Christopher Walken

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:18.767
was just cast
in "Dune: Part II."

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:19.968
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.601
[ Cheering and applause ]
He's playing the emperor,

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:23.167
alongside Timothée Chalamet

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:24.667
and Zendaya,
who are coming back,

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.567
so I thought it'd be fun
to go around the studio

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.133
and see who could do
the best impression

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.067
of Christopher Walken in "Dune."

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:31.467
Alright, here, I'll go first.

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:32.534
[ Clears throat ]
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:34.234
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.133
[ As Walken ]
The spice must flow.

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:37.067
[ Applause ]

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:38.334
Felt good.
-Yeah.

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:40.834
-Higgins.
Higgins, let's hear your best

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:42.000
"Dune" Christopher Walken.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.400
-Alright, ready?
-Yeah.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.434
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:46.934
[ As Walken ]
Fear is the mind-killer.

00:04:46.934 --> 00:04:48.834
[ Cheering and applause ]
Oh.

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:51.434
That's actually better
than I thought.

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:54.100
James, let's hear your Walken.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.000
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:55.834
[ As Walken ]
If you walk

00:04:55.834 --> 00:04:57.400
without rhythm...

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.334
[ Laughter ]
...you sound a lot
like my friend --

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.934
[ Sputtering ]
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.667
...Smooth Jeffrey.

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:07.534
We've been friends
since he was 30 years old.

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:09.701
Now, he's 31 years old.

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:10.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:12.501
He's a really bad dancer.

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:13.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:14.834
But he invites me to go

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.734
to the clubs with him, anyway.

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:18.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:23.133
He said he won't be my friend
anymore, if I don't.

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:26.300
Let's face it --
I'm not exactly in a position

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.834
to be choosy
in the friends department.

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:32.167
Smooth Jeffrey's signature move
is called The Flop.

00:05:32.167 --> 00:05:33.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:34.367
I --

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:36.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:39.434
I'd show you how
to do it right now,

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:41.801
but I'm not wearing
the right kind of pants.

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:44.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.267
-Wow.

00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:49.234
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.367
Smooth Jeffrey.

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:54.901
-Alright.
Moving on,

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:57.300
[ Laughter ]
got some sports news.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:01.367
Some sports news.

00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:03.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:06.000
-What was it called, The Flop?
-I don't know what he --

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.434
-He started going off --
-He started going off

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:08.267
on his own tangent.
-Smooth Jeffrey.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.234
I don't know what's going on.

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:12.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:13.834
Here's what we did --
James rehearsed

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:14.968
a different bit earlier today.

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:16.067
We just added those cards,

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:17.200
just to see if he'd read them.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.133
It's making us laugh.

00:06:21.133 --> 00:06:23.834
[ Cheering ]

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:26.234
[ Claps ]

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.334
Rehearsal,
it was like two lines?

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:32.767
-One or two.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:33.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:35.067
It's like eight cards.
-Yeah.

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:37.968
Guys, moving on,
some sports news --

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:40.334
Rich Strike,
the 80-to-1 long shot horse

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:41.634
that just won
the Kentucky Derby,

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.367
is skipping the next race
in the Triple Crown

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:46.133
and coming back
for the third race.

00:06:46.133 --> 00:06:47.534
[ Murmuring ]
Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:47.534 --> 00:06:49.000
Honestly, there's nothing
more relatable

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.400
than exercising for two minutes
and then taking a month off.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:54.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:55.667 --> 00:06:57.701
It's a little suspect,
though, right?

00:06:57.701 --> 00:06:59.968
I mean, it's not a good sign
when you have a shocking win,

00:06:59.968 --> 00:07:01.634
then suddenly need
to lay low for a while.

00:07:01.634 --> 00:07:02.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.934 --> 00:07:05.300
And, finally,
a company called Plufl

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:08.400
has created the world's
first human-sized dog bed

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.801
and it costs $400.

00:07:09.801 --> 00:07:11.534
[ Laughter ]
Here it is.

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:13.567
[ Ohs and applause ]
-Wow.

00:07:13.567 --> 00:07:14.868
Honestly, I can't tell
what's more annoying --

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:16.767
the bed, the price,
or that I just had to say

00:07:16.767 --> 00:07:17.667
the word Plufl.

00:07:17.667 --> 00:07:18.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.868 --> 00:07:20.534
Yep, Plufl.
Yeah, it sounds like

00:07:20.534 --> 00:07:22.601
a dating app
for single dogs in your area.

00:07:22.601 --> 00:07:25.100
[ Laughter ]
Can we see it again?

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:28.100
Yeah. For the low,
reasonable price of $400,

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.634
you can live just like your dog.

00:07:29.634 --> 00:07:31.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.100
Very easy to use.
Just get in,

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.601
turn around three times...
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:36.467
...turn around three more times
the other way,

00:07:36.467 --> 00:07:37.934
lie down,
and dream about rabbits.

00:07:37.934 --> 00:07:39.133
[ Applause ]
We have a great show tonight.

